WEBVTT

00:12.970 --> 00:18.710
Hikari ga sasu sora, umareochiru kage
In the bright sky illuminated by
sunlight, darkened shadows are born.

00:18.810 --> 00:24.150
Unmei wa dokomademo hikisakareru
Fate itself is being torn apart.

00:25.190 --> 00:30.150
Donna toki mo kesshite akiramenainara
If you never give up, no matter what happens,

00:30.330 --> 00:37.560
mada tozasareteru tobira kanarazu hiraku
Even that locked door will open for you.

00:38.530 --> 00:43.990
Eien datte dakishimete, fuuin mo tokihanachi
Embrace eternity and release the seal.

00:44.070 --> 00:49.940
Mamorubekimono ga ima kokoni wa arukara
Because the ones you wish
to protect are right here.

00:49.940 --> 00:55.880
Namida mo gyutto dakishimete,
yasashisa de tsutsumikomi
Embrace their tears with kindness.

00:55.880 --> 01:01.560
Nagareru mizu no youni tsuyoku nare
Become strong like the formless water,

01:01.560 --> 01:07.550
omouyouni tsuyoku nare
Become as strong as you wish to be.

01:07.700 --> 01:13.170
Mou jibun ni obienaide
Stop being afraid of yourself.

01:13.170 --> 01:19.800
Sou mirai wo osorenaide
Do not fear the future.

01:35.020 --> 01:37.150
Spring cleaning?

01:37.260 --> 01:39.780
We need to get it done before the New Year.

01:40.300 --> 01:41.630
You better not slack off.

01:42.960 --> 01:44.690
I'll do the kitchen.

01:45.200 --> 01:47.000
Toru will do the living room.

01:47.500 --> 01:49.440
Ko, you're in charge of the bath and toilet.

01:49.870 --> 01:52.240
Ku, you do the front door and hallways.

01:52.940 --> 01:57.940
Our Fox Deity, Goes to the New Year's Festival

02:00.920 --> 02:05.110
I finally get to clean the places
I'm usually too busy for!

02:05.450 --> 02:10.320
I have twice the number of workers
this year so it should be easier...

02:13.030 --> 02:15.000
Why am I doing this?

02:18.130 --> 02:21.190
Ku! What are you doing? Stop messing around!

02:26.770 --> 02:28.110
What happened here, Ko?!

02:28.440 --> 02:33.110
I used extra detergent since we
are doing the spring cleaning.

02:33.250 --> 02:34.840
You're using way too much!

02:35.520 --> 02:37.920
You're just making more work for me!

02:38.450 --> 02:40.890
Why is it still wet here?

02:41.090 --> 02:42.390
Are you sure you wiped it down?

02:42.560 --> 02:43.520
Yes, I did.

02:44.030 --> 02:46.290
I'll do the rest here. Can you go out
to sweep the front door?

02:46.690 --> 02:50.060
Ko, I'll do the toilet so go help Toru.

02:50.670 --> 02:51.360
All right.

03:00.510 --> 03:05.240
Ku! Be sure to put all the
trash and leaves in a bag!

03:05.580 --> 03:06.880
Yeah yeah.

03:17.790 --> 03:18.990
How's the living room?

03:19.190 --> 03:20.090
I'm done.

03:20.090 --> 03:20.960
We are done.

03:22.630 --> 03:24.330
Man, I'm tired.

03:24.400 --> 03:26.070
I'm done with the front door.

03:26.070 --> 03:27.860
All right. Time to check.

03:31.510 --> 03:32.500
What's this?

03:34.080 --> 03:38.510
"Suzunose Mochi Making Contest.
10 free mochi for every participant."

03:38.850 --> 03:41.140
"However, only 2 participants per household."

03:41.280 --> 03:42.150
Mochi!

03:42.420 --> 03:45.610
Oh, right. I didn't buy the
mochi for New Year's yet.

03:45.990 --> 03:47.650
That's great. I should check it out!

03:48.520 --> 03:49.680
I'm going with Toru.

03:51.290 --> 03:53.280
Ku and Ko, you're staying to watch the house.

03:53.760 --> 03:57.000
I'll make you some red bean soup
with the freshly made mochi.

03:57.000 --> 03:59.090
Yay, red bean soup!

04:00.100 --> 04:03.000
20 pieces means there are 4 for each of us!

04:05.910 --> 04:07.930
It should be around here.

04:08.180 --> 04:10.580
They're holding a mochi-making event here?

04:10.650 --> 04:13.170
I should have the right date and time...

04:21.490 --> 04:26.950
Where's my mochi? Where is it?

04:27.230 --> 04:28.490
They are taking a while.

04:32.930 --> 04:33.800
Tenko-sama?

04:36.740 --> 04:38.230
A mochi-making event?

04:39.810 --> 04:41.240
Didn't hear anything about that.

04:47.020 --> 04:47.950
Tenko-sama!

04:57.390 --> 04:58.320
It's a Dema.

04:59.230 --> 05:00.520
Let's follow the trail of mud.

05:00.900 --> 05:01.490
Yes.

05:21.750 --> 05:24.720
Could Noboru-sama and Toru-sama be in here?

05:25.090 --> 05:27.080
Is that you Ko?! Is Ku with you?!

05:27.220 --> 05:29.020
Ku-chan! Ko-chan!

05:30.760 --> 05:32.690
Noboru! Toru! Stand back!

05:32.890 --> 05:33.660
All right.

05:34.160 --> 05:34.860
Mamorime.

05:35.060 --> 05:35.650
Yes.

06:20.810 --> 06:23.070
Gyokuyo! I know you're here! Show yourself!

06:25.750 --> 06:26.770
Gyokuyo!

06:33.050 --> 06:33.920
Tenko-sama!

06:34.090 --> 06:35.450
Please stop!

06:38.760 --> 06:40.090
How can you be so stupid?!

06:41.800 --> 06:44.290
You're the one being stupid!

06:45.570 --> 06:47.470
Let Noboru and Toru out of there!

06:47.940 --> 06:52.100
I only sealed them. They'll have
a taste of what they did to you!

06:52.270 --> 06:55.830
I told you the last time!
I don't hold a grudge against them!

06:56.140 --> 06:57.480
But I do!

06:57.850 --> 06:59.510
Why do you have to do that?!

06:59.650 --> 07:00.580
Do what?

07:00.780 --> 07:04.880
They yelled at you and made
you sweep! You're a tenko!

07:07.760 --> 07:08.810
What's so funny?!

07:08.960 --> 07:10.980
You're right.

07:11.660 --> 07:16.390
I wondered why I had to help clean, too.

07:16.800 --> 07:21.600
But I'm enjoying everything, including that.

07:21.870 --> 07:25.600
Is this a part of those "good memories"
you talked about?

07:25.870 --> 07:26.900
That's rubbish!

07:28.340 --> 07:29.680
Free Noboru and Toru!

07:29.680 --> 07:30.580
No!

07:33.920 --> 07:34.520
Why?!

07:34.520 --> 07:36.750
Just do it! Free Noboru and Toru!

07:38.320 --> 07:39.150
Why?!

07:43.590 --> 07:46.290
Are those humans more
important to you than me?!

08:04.950 --> 08:06.280
Please stop.

08:10.820 --> 08:13.250
Fine. I'll let them go.

08:14.560 --> 08:15.820
But on one condition!

08:16.020 --> 08:16.790
What condition?

08:17.230 --> 08:20.720
You'll have to leave them.

08:20.960 --> 08:24.130
Unless you do that, I will hate
them for as long as I live.

08:24.670 --> 08:27.000
I'll think they are looking down on you.

08:27.270 --> 08:30.430
And that will make me take out
my anger on them.

08:30.670 --> 08:35.010
Besides, those two have had
nothing but trouble since you came!

08:36.240 --> 08:41.180
They find yokai that ordinary humans would
never see and get caught in their messes!

08:42.020 --> 08:45.180
It's better for you to be gone! For their sake, too!

08:46.490 --> 08:48.460
Even if you're having fun being with them!

08:53.060 --> 08:56.720
Fine. I'll leave the Takagami household.

08:58.030 --> 09:02.030
So don't you ever do anything to Noboru or Toru.

09:04.140 --> 09:04.760
Dema.

09:09.640 --> 09:11.310
Noboru-sama! Toru-sama!

09:11.480 --> 09:13.000
We're finally free...

09:13.150 --> 09:16.550
That mochi-making event was a lie!

09:18.050 --> 09:18.810
Who's that?

09:19.450 --> 09:20.350
Tama-chan!

09:23.060 --> 09:24.080
Where's Ku-chan?

09:24.660 --> 09:26.790
Kugen has left you for good.

09:28.200 --> 09:29.360
That was the deal.

09:29.460 --> 09:29.990
What?!

09:30.260 --> 09:33.360
Why would you be so mean, Tama-chan?!

09:33.500 --> 09:35.330
You will never understand.

09:43.810 --> 09:45.070
Ku-chan...

09:49.820 --> 09:50.410
Ku!

09:54.320 --> 09:55.650
Tenko-sama!

10:07.170 --> 10:09.660
Where did Ku-chan go?

10:10.270 --> 10:12.430
Maybe Ku already left Suzunose.

10:44.840 --> 10:46.240
It's been a while.

10:46.340 --> 10:47.070
Uh-huh.

10:54.020 --> 10:54.670
Hey!

11:04.430 --> 11:05.450
Grandma!

11:06.530 --> 11:07.760
Good evening!

11:08.000 --> 11:09.290
It has been a while.

11:09.660 --> 11:11.890
Sorry for coming all of a sudden. So about...

11:12.200 --> 11:13.630
You mean the tenko Kugen?

11:13.630 --> 11:15.070
Is Ku back?

11:15.440 --> 11:16.600
Probably.

11:17.200 --> 11:20.040
I sensed its presence,
but I haven't seen it personally.

11:20.040 --> 11:20.780
Let's go!

11:20.780 --> 11:21.240
Yeah!

11:27.720 --> 11:30.480
Do you think Ku-chan will come back?

11:39.930 --> 11:41.200
What's wrong, Ko?

11:41.200 --> 11:42.360
Nothing.

11:44.430 --> 11:45.690
Noboru, we're here!

11:58.810 --> 11:59.550
Ku!

11:59.550 --> 12:00.640
Ku-chan!

12:02.320 --> 12:03.350
We came for you!

12:03.350 --> 12:04.340
Let's go home.

12:05.290 --> 12:09.420
I'm tired of slaving away for you two.

12:10.390 --> 12:13.920
Besides, why should a tenko
have to help you clean?

12:14.100 --> 12:16.430
I want to return to a carefree life.

12:16.860 --> 12:18.830
I'm free now.

12:19.870 --> 12:20.970
Ku-chan...

12:20.970 --> 12:26.240
I'm sick of being ordered
around and yelled at by you.

12:27.880 --> 12:28.770
Ku-chan...

12:29.110 --> 12:32.910
You're only doing this because
you promised Tama-chan, right?

12:33.080 --> 12:38.310
You promised to leave us so
Tama-chan would stop coming after us.

12:39.390 --> 12:41.750
I understand how Tama-chan feels.

12:41.990 --> 12:47.090
If anyone locked up Noboru,
I'd be mad at whoever did it.

12:47.600 --> 12:48.290
Toru.

12:48.830 --> 12:51.530
But I want to be friends with Tama-chan, too.

12:51.700 --> 12:53.830
You two are siblings, right?

12:54.140 --> 12:57.160
That's why I want Tama-chan to like us.

12:57.510 --> 12:59.230
I want all of us to be family.

13:00.040 --> 13:02.740
I'm sorry for making you protect us all the time.

13:03.110 --> 13:07.670
But we'll try to become stronger.
So please come home.

13:11.720 --> 13:13.740
Ku, we'll be waiting.

13:13.950 --> 13:15.080
Noboru.

13:15.660 --> 13:19.350
We'll wait outside the shrine until you come out.

13:34.580 --> 13:37.640
I guess I didn't really think
this through. Are you cold?

13:37.910 --> 13:38.440
Nah.

13:39.150 --> 13:40.910
I'm getting hungry, too.

13:41.180 --> 13:42.050
Yeah.

13:42.650 --> 13:43.910
Maybe we should go back once.

13:44.490 --> 13:45.350
No.

13:49.390 --> 13:51.820
I came to check on you because
you were taking so long.

13:52.190 --> 13:54.060
I'm sorry, Uncle Tatsuhiko.

13:54.530 --> 13:55.590
Where's the tenko-sama?

13:56.000 --> 13:58.760
We found Ku-chan. But Ku-chan
doesn't want to go home.

13:58.930 --> 14:03.200
Oh. Then why don't you go back for
tonight and come back tomorrow?

14:03.340 --> 14:05.100
No, we'll wait here.

14:06.310 --> 14:10.400
Ku-chan left home to protect us.

14:11.780 --> 14:15.370
All right. Then I'll bring some food for you.

14:16.150 --> 14:20.590
Oh yeah. I have some more stuff I want you
to bring, Uncle Tatsuhiko.

14:31.700 --> 14:33.890
Ku! The red bean soup is done!

14:34.240 --> 14:38.270
It's sweet and warm! Freshly made!

14:38.270 --> 14:39.610
It's really good!

14:39.610 --> 14:43.480
Trying to lure me with food?
Who do they think I am?

14:43.710 --> 14:49.580
If you want to be so stubborn, you won't get
the New Year's soba, osechi, or even the zoni!

14:53.920 --> 14:55.010
Noboru...

14:55.560 --> 14:57.290
Let's start eating.

15:05.830 --> 15:07.770
I'm eating, too.

15:09.470 --> 15:11.270
What about the New Year's soba and osechi?

15:11.270 --> 15:12.470
Of course!

15:13.570 --> 15:16.240
All right! My Amano-Iwato plan worked!

15:16.740 --> 15:18.810
I knew you'd fall for this.

15:18.810 --> 15:20.680
This is all mine!

15:21.350 --> 15:23.150
Or else I'm not going home!

15:24.320 --> 15:26.950
Well, I'll give a bowl to Toru.

15:26.950 --> 15:28.360
Come on!

15:28.360 --> 15:31.490
You're always telling me what to do
so I'm having my revenge today!

15:31.490 --> 15:33.360
I'm making sure you're not getting any!

15:33.590 --> 15:34.600
I'm the one who made it!

15:34.600 --> 15:34.930
What would Miyako say if she saw this?

15:34.930 --> 15:35.960
Give it back!
What would Miyako say if she saw this?

15:35.960 --> 15:37.030
What would Miyako say if she saw this?

15:37.030 --> 15:37.230
Let go!
What would Miyako say if she saw this?

15:37.230 --> 15:37.530
Let go!

15:37.530 --> 15:38.070
Let go!
I think she'd be happy to see it.

15:38.070 --> 15:39.530
I think she'd be happy to see it.

15:39.830 --> 15:41.630
Let go or I won't make any soba for you!

15:43.600 --> 15:45.070
Maybe...

15:45.070 --> 15:47.060
Why did you let go all of a sudden?!

15:50.810 --> 15:52.180
The red bean soup is hot!

15:52.180 --> 15:52.980
Of course it's hot!

15:52.980 --> 15:54.570
It's burning me!

16:02.660 --> 16:03.620
Welcome home.

16:11.200 --> 16:12.460
This is for the New Year's offering.

16:12.670 --> 16:17.690
I'd never give an offering to Ebisu's shrine,
but I'm fine with this place!

16:28.150 --> 16:30.580
Ku-chan! Ko-chan! What did you wish for?!

16:30.820 --> 16:33.850
I wished for your health, but as for me...

16:33.850 --> 16:37.220
I want to do everything
briskly and in a snap and...

16:37.220 --> 16:39.530
- Okay, we get it...
...glittery and twirling and...

16:39.530 --> 16:39.690
...fizzing and dazzling...

16:39.690 --> 16:40.890
- Takagami!
...fizzing and dazzling...

16:40.890 --> 16:41.030
...fizzing and dazzling...

16:41.030 --> 16:42.150
Hey!
...fizzing and dazzling...

16:47.470 --> 16:49.800
Takagami, Happy New Year!

16:49.800 --> 16:51.070
Happy New Year.

16:51.840 --> 16:54.100
I hope the next year will be great!

16:54.840 --> 16:57.330
Sakura, don't you mean this year?

16:59.710 --> 17:02.520
I hope Takagami will finally notice this year.

17:02.520 --> 17:03.980
Sakura's feelings toward him...

17:04.250 --> 17:05.650
But I doubt it.

17:06.990 --> 17:08.750
You look good in that kimono, Sakura.

17:08.920 --> 17:11.230
Takagami complimented me
on the first day of the year!

17:11.230 --> 17:15.420
I'm so glad I woke up early to wear this kimono!

17:16.000 --> 17:18.620
Maybe Ko and Ku should
have worn a kimono, too.

17:19.270 --> 17:21.200
You're turning to them?
Is that what you really mean?!

17:21.570 --> 17:26.030
He just wanted to see Ko-chan
or Tenko-san in a kimono?!

17:28.110 --> 17:30.510
Happy New Year, Noboru-kun!

17:31.510 --> 17:32.600
Happy New Year.

17:32.850 --> 17:36.680
We're holding a New Year's party!
Daddy is back, too!

17:36.680 --> 17:39.020
Oh, really? That's great.

17:39.020 --> 17:41.650
You should come!
I want to introduce you to Daddy.

17:42.620 --> 17:44.060
"Introduce you to Daddy?"

17:44.160 --> 17:48.820
No! I can't let that happen! Takagami
might end up engaged to Miyabe-san!

17:49.200 --> 17:52.320
Don't go! Don't go with her, Takagami!

17:52.630 --> 17:56.900
We're doing a New Year's party of our own.
We're having hot pot with the family.

17:57.300 --> 17:59.070
Really? That's too bad.

17:59.710 --> 18:00.730
Then let me give you this!

18:01.280 --> 18:02.740
It's a charm from a god of matchmaking.

18:03.410 --> 18:04.900
I hope this year will be great!

18:09.350 --> 18:11.820
Why would she give me a
charm for matchmaking?

18:12.020 --> 18:13.820
He really doesn't get it at all.

18:13.820 --> 18:15.250
He's hopeless.

18:16.820 --> 18:19.760
What's going on?! You came to my
shrine for the New Year's festival?

18:19.760 --> 18:20.660
Mubyo-san!

18:20.960 --> 18:22.860
Great to see you here!

18:22.860 --> 18:25.170
Why do women keep flocking to him?!

18:25.170 --> 18:27.070
Is he cursed or something?!

18:27.070 --> 18:29.800
Sounds like a curse I'd want to have.

18:31.270 --> 18:33.330
Happy New Year to you.

18:33.670 --> 18:35.300
Same to you.

18:36.680 --> 18:38.700
Another woman!

18:38.880 --> 18:42.820
Why? Why? Why?!

18:45.950 --> 18:48.290
Happy New Year!

18:52.030 --> 18:53.830
Tenko-sama, you're in a kimono!

18:53.830 --> 18:55.620
You look very elegant!

18:55.900 --> 18:59.490
The Mamorime helped me
dress in one of Miyako's.

18:59.630 --> 19:02.400
It really feels like New Year's
when I see you in that.

19:02.400 --> 19:04.460
You look wonderful in that also, Mamorime.

19:06.640 --> 19:11.100
First take a look at the color of the stock.

19:12.410 --> 19:18.370
It's my own special recipe using shaved bonito.

19:20.550 --> 19:21.450
Ku-chan?

19:21.690 --> 19:23.180
I need to go get someone.

19:23.490 --> 19:24.650
Who?

19:31.770 --> 19:32.860
I know you're there.

19:35.370 --> 19:37.800
I'm sorry I broke our promise.

19:43.540 --> 19:44.670
Gyokuyo.

19:46.610 --> 19:49.580
I don't understand you.

19:50.120 --> 19:52.950
Why you would protect the
family who sealed you?

19:55.290 --> 19:59.490
But it's a bit more clear to me now.
You were just having fun.

20:00.390 --> 20:02.090
Because you were alone all this time...

20:03.600 --> 20:05.860
...you liked being with a family.

20:06.600 --> 20:07.590
Maybe.

20:08.300 --> 20:11.860
Why don't you come?
We're holding a hot pot party right now.

20:11.970 --> 20:13.870
Noboru and Toru would love to see you there.

20:14.110 --> 20:15.270
Why would I go?!

20:15.580 --> 20:17.310
Come on! It's New Year's!

20:17.310 --> 20:18.300
Let me go!

20:18.450 --> 20:20.540
You're my family, too.

20:22.680 --> 20:24.820
Why don't you try on a
kimono to get into the spirit?!

20:24.820 --> 20:25.790
What?!

20:25.790 --> 20:26.720
- Yeah, that's a great idea!

20:26.720 --> 20:27.550
- Stop it!
- Yeah, that's a great idea!

20:27.550 --> 20:28.560
Get them to dress you up!

20:28.560 --> 20:28.890
- Why?!

20:28.890 --> 20:31.160
- There were lots of different kinds of kimono!
- Why?!

20:31.160 --> 20:32.230
Stop it!

20:32.230 --> 20:34.660
The Mamorime will help you wear it, so let's go!

20:59.220 --> 21:04.490
Hare mo ke mo naku oowarawa de neboketerarenai
With all the commotion, I can't stay still.

21:05.030 --> 21:10.520
Kidoairaku gochamaze aa ijou
With emotions running wild,
everything seems so odd.

21:10.830 --> 21:16.360
Inochimijikashi toiunonara hara wo kukutte
Life is short so be prepared for anything.

21:16.640 --> 21:21.780
Iran kyoukai nanno sono yuke
Transcend that useless boundary and go!

21:21.780 --> 21:22.430
Kitsune Soba

21:22.810 --> 21:28.480
kingin kagayaku suteki na mainichi
With those bright days behind you,

21:28.620 --> 21:34.420
omatsurisawagi de mairouka
It's time for some merrymaking.

21:34.990 --> 21:40.820
Sora ni hi wo tomoshi tamashii no pareedo
Light the skies for this parade of souls,

21:40.990 --> 21:46.690
shiawase no kotodama hora kousa suru
The kotodama of happiness crosses paths.

21:46.830 --> 21:52.430
Namida mo wasurete odori odore
Forget those tears and dance away,

21:52.670 --> 21:58.580
toriaezu iiyone tanoshikeryasa
Forget about everything else
since we're having fun now.

22:06.650 --> 22:11.530
Now then, dip your thinly sliced winter
yellowtail into the golden stock.

22:11.530 --> 22:16.860
Then eat it with your spicy
grated daikon radish and ponzu.

22:24.100 --> 22:26.940
Let me formally introduce you. This is Gyokuyo.

22:30.680 --> 22:33.010
Happy New Year, Tama-chan!

22:33.980 --> 22:35.170
Tama-chan!

22:35.420 --> 22:37.540
Tenko-sama and her look almost identical.

22:38.790 --> 22:40.850
That's because they're brothers.

22:40.850 --> 22:42.850
Wait, should I call them sisters?

22:43.260 --> 22:44.810
Here, have a seat.

22:47.730 --> 22:49.630
Eat up!

22:49.960 --> 22:51.660
Tama, here's your ponzu.

22:53.130 --> 22:54.100
Tama?

22:54.100 --> 22:55.800
That's like a cat's name.

22:55.800 --> 22:57.170
My name is Gyokuyo.

22:57.170 --> 22:59.000
But that's why I call you Tama-chan.

22:59.140 --> 23:02.010
Noboru-sama, what if you
added a "-chan" to her name?

23:02.080 --> 23:03.630
She doesn't need it!

23:03.810 --> 23:06.180
Come on, Tama. Eat up! It's good!

23:07.650 --> 23:09.880
You only need to let it swim
in the stock for a little while.

23:09.880 --> 23:13.410
Okay, it's done. Now take it out. Now!

23:13.650 --> 23:16.920
Take some veggies from
around here to eat with it.

23:19.760 --> 23:20.490
This is good!

23:20.760 --> 23:26.130
I would like to emphasize that timing
is everything when it comes to hot pot.

23:26.130 --> 23:29.200
That's why... Hey, that's too much sauce!

23:29.200 --> 23:32.970
Pay some respect to my secret recipe stock...

23:32.970 --> 23:34.980
Do it this way and...

23:34.980 --> 23:37.710
I love New Year's!
